# Without this, a build from a working tree picks up whatever caches happen to be lying around
# and produces a different digest than a build from a clean `git archive` checkout - which would
# make "the image reproduces" depend on whether someone ran the tests first. Found by the
# Reproduction Agent, whose working-tree build differed from its clean-checkout build by four
# stray __pycache__ files.
#
# The `**/` prefixes are load-bearing. Docker ignore patterns match against paths relative to
# the context ROOT, so a bare `__pycache__/` matches only a top-level one and silently misses
# `harness/__pycache__/`. Measured: without `**/`, a contaminated tree still produced a
# different digest (2226698c...) than a clean one (5a302f2f...).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.DS_Store
